# Git workflow: production only

- Commit and push directly to `production`, the canonical branch of `remondevries/backsteros`. No pull requests, no feature branches, no sub-branches.
- Never open a PR or create a branch unless the person who gave you the task explicitly asks for one.
- Before every push, run from the repo root and push only if all pass: `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint`, `pnpm test`, `pnpm test:integration` (integration uses Docker Postgres DB `backsteros_test`, never live `backsteros`). If you touched `backsterdev/`, also run `vp run -r typecheck` and `vp run -r test` there.
- If anything fails, fix it locally and rerun before pushing. Never push red and never skip or disable a test to get green.
- CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) also runs on pushes to `production` (mobile excluded), but only after the push lands. Local runs are the gate.
- `git pull --rebase origin production` before pushing; rerun the suite if that pulled in new commits.

Full rule: root `AGENTS.md`, section "Git workflow (non-negotiable)".
